  "structure": {
    "block_count": 43,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Molar Pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "37f16753190e7accaed0aaa39ddef38396b2347cc41666f2640a7cab79426ce8",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "molar pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "059fd5f4b31d59aac44b06bc16f01af0c9673ca0902335c63c59147f08d2fcbe",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "An error in conception can produce this abnormal (and rare) condition.",
        "text_sha256": "3bba6f1c97a4f6d20c6cbdd3bb74269badf9a5008117457a898db95068316670",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pregnancy is always incredibly difficult, even if it happens very early on. A molar pregnancy, though rare, is one of the reasons a pregnancy might end prematurely. Learn more about what a molar pregnancy is and what causes it.",
        "text_sha256": "33bfbce5f48b23f281106e9225e312ead08bb3a096cf5acde917bddff76a0128",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is a molar pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "ddfa10a8d217ed86a4fc710daef02405fffb49d168b28acb40aa6df04c2ac82f",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Molar Pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "37f16753190e7accaed0aaa39ddef38396b2347cc41666f2640a7cab79426ce8",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In a molar pregnancy (also called a hydatidiform mole), the tissue that’s meant to become the placenta overgrows, becoming a mass of cysts.",
        "text_sha256": "bc15559b463fc7368f75bfa2e7eed4138369641b3c568e9f97cb6cce273b13e6",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In some cases there is no accompanying embryo, while in other cases, a partially formed but not viable fetus or some identifiable embryonic or fetal tissue is present. This is called a partial molar pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "a625e63aca031fd44b01eb118fdae711363b82a361bd48353e6ea74fcaefe9b0",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Complete molar pregnancy vs. partial molar pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "dc5325513d1ab22b017e4734d434d1966cffe1278cb1f4d44cd684180c1341cf",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The cause of a molar pregnancy is an abnormality during fertilization, likely when two sets of chromosomes from the father become mixed in with either one set of chromosomes from the mother (partial mole) — or none of her chromosomes at all (complete mole).",
        "text_sha256": "ef18c825b8c6eb6d3590d8c20e1064fcc5ae44c587cc813c4a8aa114da9724fa",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Most molar pregnancies are discovered within weeks of conception, and unfortunately all end in miscarriage .",
        "text_sha256": "83854a356aca903d7480e7691b2b7dc942c7b444521055f59dbc9be429a21389",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How common are molar pregnancies?",
        "text_sha256": "8667a42888352d667a8d3526a23ef03634c43f6f18cb1964065483fad6f0b13b",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Luckily, molar pregnancies are relatively rare, occurring only in 1 out of 1,000 pregnancies. Trusted SourceMayo ClinicMolar PregnancySee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "b2315b938da0c84148cc5f2837ac459084c4184bc5b24e28b635be3827221482",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Molar Pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "37f16753190e7accaed0aaa39ddef38396b2347cc41666f2640a7cab79426ce8",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Who is most at risk of having a molar pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "5edf8864529cdcfe3e8d7c83f834bbd3ac156eba3dcfddc498b29cebd99008e7",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Women who are at slightly increased risk for a molar pregnancy include those over the age of 35, those under age 20 and those who have had multiple miscarriages.",
        "text_sha256": "1923db8ab5829b66ee167c9879a52e5d38376ba99d5046128821eb3cadf076a7",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What are the symptoms of a molar pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "0f1a1103d5311e04d454708627f0d8d76d50b9e0040edc70fad3fbfaf0ac6e86",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The symptoms of a molar pregnancy can include:",
        "text_sha256": "6f8b46ecfac15dec8745e944db9b526797a7ba893add6f7182d79cae6c5d65ee",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A continuous or intermittent brown or bright red, bloody discharge (the most common symptom)",
        "text_sha256": "67dcc0d142d1798a00a0907d8d4e93835a85c16cc5069b790288d29a86efe969",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Vaginal bleeding",
        "text_sha256": "85233c7d13afe71916ae3329612cdeba907321dd01b559d2270d6bec95fdd975",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Severe nausea and vomiting",
        "text_sha256": "ba187b456889d57311afd4efe0e56b3c1663dab9980543d8f8b0b63e47d0b4f0",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Uncomfortable cramping",
        "text_sha256": "cbf5a556b8d416e32d0150679839c2c74622984a1a5128c16fe63be2c53e64ff",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Unexplained weight loss",
        "text_sha256": "2c47fed59d7d24c55782871099dc5bc8483af208801cccda337ebca2b13eb144",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "High blood pressure",
        "text_sha256": "dccf72d95ec49983ff7ff0124b99215c0c00c71da9ce90f28a96aae73fe36f87",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Larger than expected uterus",
        "text_sha256": "29cedf64f7dbf043502ba8dc8cc74b85c8d50a40594ec8ed1c7b9c24d6884834",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Doughy uterus (rather than firm)",
        "text_sha256": "268ae970f2b1adb0a343914f96c6db22d7c4f60a68c125a9174b3ce788d64bb7",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Absence of embryonic or fetal tissue (as seen on ultrasound)",
        "text_sha256": "3efb8deb2cfd1f54d9210d93f4681b3c89931df03f3f18c886f66c2bcc602408",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Excessive levels of thyroid hormone",
        "text_sha256": "0ee3d7b30cc86257c391896d983a2bc75d3f0b9c54ac180dd88ef290fbb1adf2",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "The passage of an oval-shaped, grape-like cyst called a trophoblast from the vagina (or multiple cysts)",
        "text_sha256": "42243c2f1aa560883fe5715b2c4a3ce20688bce435f94c48a4b57ac08cf7e664",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Ovarian cysts (detected by your doctor)",
        "text_sha256": "4d1adc4b5abcbdfb97eaf73c08b5512ffafdf16c3e308a2391d2fbfbc8066643",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Preeclampsia (usually not discovered until you make an appointment with your doctor)",
        "text_sha256": "d576dce184347911779f15d5d2d1377568f4051c4ec750a3302db395c36a6080",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Should you be concerned if you think you've had a molar pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "a4c2f28f1e6c0f68a0174cc7f1b0ceaaa452f1d92e8335ab89acb70ce8ade008",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A molar pregnancy is a risk factor for the development of persistent gestational trophoblastic neoplasia (GTN). Also known as gestational trophoblastic disease, this condition is when left-behind placental tissues continue to grow. Trusted SourceAmerican Cancer SocietyAbout Gestational Trophoblastic DiseaseSee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "acb4f15263fbff4ff3194c18f9fbde6f9077340ce8c39b1357c9dc9588bc2482",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Cancer SocietyAbout Gestational Trophoblastic DiseaseSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "624f0cbf4fa6ebe4681cd7d3dc691328b3917cd2ce523d5fed827494c9692346",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Very occasionally, that can lead to a rare form of cancer known as choriocarcinoma . Fortunately, GTN and choriocarcinoma are extremely uncommon conditions, with the latter occurring in only 1 out of every 40,000 pregnancies.",
        "text_sha256": "4e334f492705549f5555132bd52399f324320ca40ae3fc16361442828d33191b",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What you can do if you think you're experiencing a molar pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "83b0d09d3aad4040bbdee7e6f9a222d8d178cfb56a633dfddc9995788ea6e68d",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Call your doctor if you experience any of the symptoms listed above. Since some of these symptoms can be difficult to differentiate from normal early pregnancy signs and symptoms , you should trust your instincts. Many completely normal pregnancies include some spotting and cramping , and most include nausea. If you think something's wrong, talk to your provider — if only to get some much-needed reassurance.",
        "text_sha256": "39d7c3c697c17f0c9028c164dacf090d0f72ab1a2272374931ac0b9b4d93561b",
        "word_count": 66
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your practitioner will likely do an ultrasound and blood work (to look at hCG levels), and he or she may want to run a chest X-ray or MRI of your abdomen. If you do have a molar pregnancy, the abnormal tissue must be removed via a dilation and curettage (D&C), a procedure that usually takes 15 to 30 minutes. Your doctor will use a speculum (the same tool used during a routine pelvic exam) to see and dilate your cervix, then remove the tissue. Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsDilation and Curettage (D&C)See All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "b230c39da709c3f432e9f0b8da7aaa8291458cceb8cc3be926911e9fe8e8c2bc",
        "word_count": 97
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsDilation and Curettage (D&C)See All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "083998d2fc9cb164d799da97a47c41c9933660e7f13d5391a3572c7a90db6f3f",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Follow-up to check your hCG levels is crucial to make sure that abnormal tissue doesn’t grow back or progress to choriocarcinoma. Luckily, the chance of a treated molar pregnancy turning malignant is extremely rare.",
        "text_sha256": "779269d8a3bcd0ae59809ead830877b168f1ef3a32c71a09d974df8f2d4df0fa",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Getting pregnant again after a molar pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "fea4e0411f853fbf6c1c3572655a67cd1d5d4e3b40900786928a94e79d40ddea",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Yourpractitioner will probably suggest that you not get pregnant for six months to a year. Women who try to conceive sooner are at greater risk for having another molar pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "311412592d5656388aec2223ede44ccffdaa1d81d8c376f83e7dda880f6c5466",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
